# switch-t210: L4T 4.9 exposes /dev/fb0 but no DRM/KMS, so frecon's drm
# probe fails and it spews "No suitable drm driver found" / "Unable to open
# drm_master_relax" / "DBus not initialized" before exiting.  Xorg drives
# the framebuffer directly (see switch-xorg-fbdev), so frecon serves no
# purpose here.
#
# boot-splash can't simply be set `manual` because `boot-services` waits on
# its `stopped` event.  Replace the main script with a no-op so the job
# still starts, exits cleanly, and emits the event.
script
  :
end script
